WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.935
-Our first guest tonight i
an Academy Award-nominated actor

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:03.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know from films like
"Batman,"

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:04.637 line:92%
"Birdman" and "Spotlight."

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:07.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can see him in
"The Trial of the Chicago 7,

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:08.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is available
on Netflix now.

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:12.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's take a look.
-Hey, Bill.

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:13.713 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Ramsey Clark.

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:19.019
-Pleased to meet you, sir.
This is Leonard Weinglass.

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:20.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mr. Weinglass.
-And Tom Hayden.

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:26.393
-Oh, I know who Tom Hayden is.
The FBI used to work for me.

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:28.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
Those two men
are senior deputies

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:29.629 line:92%
with the Justice Department.

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:32.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's Mr. Calley
and Mr. Ackerman.

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:35.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I don't know why
these men are here.

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:37.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I invited them.
-You invited them?

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:40.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't want the appearance
of impropriety.

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:41.608 line:92%
-There isn't any impropriety

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:43.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And now there
are witnesses to that.

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:44.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please welcome back
to the show

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:46.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of our favorites,
Michael Keaton.

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:48.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
How are you, Michael?
-Hey, man.

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:49.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
How are you doing?
-I'm good.

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:53.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, it's --
-Before we start, just be fair

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:55.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ] Okay.
You know what?

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:57.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm glad you said that.
You know what?

00:00:57.557 --> 00:01:00.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because these were going to be
real tough ones.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:01.394 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:06.833 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Round the corner,
round the corner and be fair

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:09.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sorry, I have this on.
I just went out for a minute

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:11.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look at this.
I want to show you something

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:12.472 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Great, I can't wait.

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:14.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Speaking of being fair,
can you see that?

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:14.874 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Yeah, look at that.

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:17.444 size:84% position:42%
-Yeah, but look at you,
speaking -- Wait, wait.

00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:19.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do I do this?
-The other way, the other way.

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.848 line:92%
What are you trying to show me

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:23.283 line:92%
-I'm trying to say look at you

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:26.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
speaking of being fair,
you're trying to hypnotize me.

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:27.420 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.922 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Look, look at you, man.

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:32.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
Some kind of
Spock hand gesture.

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:32.992 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-It's been really --

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:34.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
I should say,
it's a great disadvantage

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:40.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I'm having no luck
hypnotizing over Zoom, nothing

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:42.569 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Man, tuna fish,

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:45.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
half a tuna fish
salad sandwich in a briefcase.

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:46.506 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Oh, man, that's funny.

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:48.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, man, that's good.
That's strong.

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:50.610 size:78% position:39%
-Thank you, Michael.
-This is odd to do --

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
By the way, can I say this
-Yeah.

00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:55.148
-This is odd to do --
Look at those hands, by the way.

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:56.583 line:92%
That's just way too much.

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:58.418 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:58.418 --> 00:01:59.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
-In the afternoon,
it feels funny.

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:05.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
It feels like this show
should be at night.

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:05.558 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I know.

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:10.296
-So I had to get some coffee
to kind of wake up a little bit.

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:14.767
-I mean, you're coming off
as a guy who is fully awake.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:17.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, good. Oh, good.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:18.705 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Good.

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:21.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's the standard.
"Yeah, he looked awake."

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:26.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, I want
to talk about --

00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:29.249 line:92%
-This barista -- barista?

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:30.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah, that's it.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:35.388
So, I went and she was --
Yeah, I was wearing this.

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:37.524 line:92%
And I'm very cautious out there,

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:40.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I ventured out
to get some coffee.

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:44.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she was really perky, like
way too perky for me

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:47.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
and really loud
when she took my order.

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:49.936
And there was a plexiglass thing
in the front and everything.

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:53.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
She was nice enough,
but she kept going "Hi!"

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:54.774 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Like, "Hi!"

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:57.443 size:75% position:38%
And she kept saying,
"What's your name?

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:58.645 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
What's your name?"

00:02:58.645 --> 00:03:01.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
Kind of like one of Santa'
helpers would say it.

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:03.850 line:92%
You know, "What's your name?

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:06.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it freaked --
and I'm kind of --

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:07.954 line:92%
when I'm out there, I'm very -

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:13.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
you could just see, like,
the COVID splashing against --

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:14.761 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:18.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was just
hitting the plexiglass.

00:03:18.598 --> 00:03:20.033 line:92%
You just want to walk out.

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:22.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
Anyway, it made me very,
very nervous.

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:22.936 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But you know what?

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:25.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're good because we've got
Scott Atlas on top of it.

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:29.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ] That's true.
Everything is under control.

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:30.443 line:92%
-Is that not the greatest name

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:33.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
Does that not sound like -
the only thing better

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:36.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
than Scott Atlas would
have been like Johnny Atlas.

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:40.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
But Scott Atlas sounds
like a teen star

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:41.721 line:92%
from the '80s, doesn't he?

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:44.757
-Yeah, it's like they gave Trump
a list of doctors

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:45.792 line:92%
and he just picked the nam

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:49.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
that sounded
like the coolest-looking dude.

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:51.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
"Hi, I'm Scott.

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.166 line:92%
Hey, gang, I'm Scott Atlas

00:03:53.166 --> 00:03:54.400 line:92%
I'll be at the Fairhaven Mal

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
this week
promoting my new album."

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:57.604 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.604 --> 00:04:01.441
-Oh, my God. The girls are going
crazy for Scott Atlas.

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:04.811 line:92%
They're lined around the block

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:07.447 line:92%
Hey, this movie is so great.

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:09.582 line:92%
And it's an Aaron Sorkin script.

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:10.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yep.
-And I have to imagine

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:12.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
as an actor,
there are just certain writers

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:16.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
where it's just a delight
to do their dialogue.

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:18.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
And not only do you
get to do Sorkin dialogue,

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:20.893 size:75% position:38%
you get to do Sorkin
courtroom dialogue,

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:21.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is maybe --
-Yeah.

00:04:21.728 --> 00:04:25.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Maybe his highest tier.
-That's right. That's right.

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:27.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's right.
That is -- That's a bump up.

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:29.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you know what else?
If you watch --

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:35.208
First of all, this cast
in this movie is so good.

00:04:35.208 --> 00:04:37.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
But if you noticed,
that's exactly right.

00:04:37.477 --> 00:04:40.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you get in the courtroo
or anything like that,

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:41.547 size:78% position:39% line:92%
it actually bumps up.

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:45.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you watch this movie
and what he does is,

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:47.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
you'll be right
in the long stretch

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:52.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
of a dramatic,
tension-filled scene.

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:58.331
And he'll just drop a gem
of a joke, a gem of a funny line

00:04:58.331 --> 00:05:03.569
and kind of, you know, boop,
lifts everything up from it.

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:05.738 line:92%
He was really fun to work with

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:09.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a really,
really terrific movie, I think

00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:10.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do want to --
because again

00:05:10.643 --> 00:05:11.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's this scene
in the courtroom.

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:15.782
And as an actor, like,
is it thrilling or intimidating?

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:18.718
I mean, just the people that are
watching you do your thing

00:05:18.718 --> 00:05:21.054 size:78% position:39%
like, Frank Langella,
Joseph Gordon-Levitt,

00:05:21.054 --> 00:05:23.723
Mark Rylance, Sacha Baron Cohen,
Jeremy Strong.

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:26.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know I'm leaving people out.
-Eddie Redmayne.

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:28.695 line:92%
-Does it make more fun or even

00:05:28.695 --> 00:05:29.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
after doing this
a long time you're like,

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:31.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, there's some real
A-listers here?"

00:05:31.898 --> 00:05:34.100 size:88% position:44%
-You know, absolutely.
That's a great question.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:36.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
Absolutely, it makes it
more fun now.

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:37.036 size:84% position:42% line:92%
You want to be in that.

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:38.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like playing
pickup basketball.

00:05:38.705 --> 00:05:39.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know?
When you say, "Yeah,

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:41.808 size:88% position:44%
I'll go down to the park
and play a little bit."

00:05:41.808 --> 00:05:42.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the whole rhythm
of everything,

00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:48.214
when everybody is so much better
or so good around you.

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:51.784
The only thing that happened
when I did the first "Batman,"

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:52.518 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
was I was very --

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:54.520 size:75% position:38%
I was pretty nervous
and self-conscious

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:57.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
about being with Jack.
-Sure, sure.

00:05:57.657 --> 00:06:00.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because he's so strong
on film, you know?

00:06:00.626 --> 00:06:04.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it ended up
just being great, you know

00:06:04.464 --> 00:06:07.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just being great.
We became pals and everything.

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:08.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
But yeah, that's
a good question.

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:09.802 line:92%
It felt pretty good actually

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:11.871
-Do you think, like,
when you think back to "Batman,"

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:13.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you saying that,
of course it makes sense.

00:06:13.239 --> 00:06:16.909
Do you think Jack Nicholson then
and throughout his career,

00:06:16.909 --> 00:06:18.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
and certainly at that poin
of his career,

00:06:18.144 --> 00:06:21.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
do you think he was aware
that people would be,

00:06:21.848 --> 00:06:23.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, intimidated
to work with him?

00:06:23.516 --> 00:06:26.386
Did he have to go out of his way
to be disarming?

00:06:26.386 --> 00:06:28.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's --
You know, I don't know.

00:06:28.187 --> 00:06:30.156
I don't know that I've eve
thought of it like that.

00:06:30.156 --> 00:06:34.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's a great --
That's a great question.

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:35.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would say, yeah,
he probably --

00:06:35.962 --> 00:06:38.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
he probably was pretty aware
of his power.

00:06:38.965 --> 00:06:44.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was so -- He had so muc
power on screen, you know, has

00:06:44.637 --> 00:06:45.338 size:78% position:39% line:92%
But it was just cool.

00:06:45.338 --> 00:06:50.743
You know, he made everybody feel
really, really relaxed.

00:06:50.743 --> 00:06:53.479
You know?
Someday in private I'll tell you

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:55.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
how he would greet
the crew in the morning.

00:06:55.782 --> 00:06:56.315 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:59.619 size:84% position:42%
Certainly can't do it
on national television.

00:06:59.619 --> 00:07:00.653 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:07:00.653 --> 00:07:03.289
Hey, by the way,
your pop's name is Larry, right?

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:04.624 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, Larry.

00:07:04.624 --> 00:07:05.992 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Hey, Larry.

00:07:05.992 --> 00:07:08.928
-There we go. Now I'm glad
we're gonna finish with this

00:07:08.928 --> 00:07:11.497 size:78% position:39%
-They're back, baby.
-He'll be very happy.

00:07:11.497 --> 00:07:15.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
5-0. We got the 5-0 Steelers
against, I think --

00:07:15.368 --> 00:07:16.569 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I guess, the 5-0 Titans.

00:07:16.569 --> 00:07:19.872
How are you feeling about
the Steelers this season?

00:07:19.872 --> 00:07:20.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Great so far.
-Yeah.

00:07:20.706 --> 00:07:23.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, this is fun so far.
We'll see.

00:07:23.876 --> 00:07:28.181
But, you know, I'm a fan of al
those teams -- Pittsburgh teams.

00:07:28.181 --> 00:07:29.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I know you've been
tweeting a lot

00:07:29.949 --> 00:07:31.717 line:92%
about Pennsylvania politics.

00:07:31.717 --> 00:07:33.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
we were mentioning Obama

00:07:33.052 --> 00:07:34.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
was there yesterday.
-Yeah.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:36.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know you were really
politically engaged

00:07:36.389 --> 00:07:37.190 line:92%
as a kid thanks to your parents.

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:40.526
Your dad -- everybody is talking
about having a plan for voting

00:07:40.526 --> 00:07:41.828 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Your dad gave you

00:07:41.828 --> 00:07:44.497 size:78% position:39%
a very specific plan
when you were voting.

00:07:44.497 --> 00:07:45.198 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, yes.

00:07:45.198 --> 00:07:46.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
My dad was commissioner
for a while.

00:07:46.966 --> 00:07:49.702 line:92%
He was very involved locally

00:07:49.702 --> 00:07:52.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, he's a working
man's Democrat.

00:07:52.738 --> 00:07:57.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was -- So it was always
in my consciousness.

00:07:57.210 --> 00:08:02.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
And just to show you
how important it is to vote,

00:08:02.748 --> 00:08:06.219
I grew up between two
kind of tough little mill towns,

00:08:06.219 --> 00:08:10.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, Coraopolis
and McKees Rocks, and --

00:08:10.089 --> 00:08:11.858 line:92%
but in the center it was rural

00:08:11.858 --> 00:08:14.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were kind of country kids
So it was small.

00:08:14.026 --> 00:08:15.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
The population was small
in the township.

00:08:15.595 --> 00:08:20.132
And my dad, when it became legal
to vote at 18,

00:08:20.132 --> 00:08:22.268 line:92%
I could not wait to vote.

00:08:22.268 --> 00:08:27.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
But my dad [Laughs]
told us how to vote.

00:08:27.073 --> 00:08:29.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
He said, "Okay, now's here's
